  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-06-15T20:41:00.319Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Right click on a node to show context menu changes node selection to that node properly. But this happens only once.\nReproduce steps:\n1. Prepare three nodes.\n2. Select 1st node.\n3. Right click on 2nd node. Then the selection changes to 2nd node.\n4. Right click on 3rd node. Then the selection remains on 2nd node. If you do delete operation, it deletes 2nd node not 3rd.\n* If you right click on free area of the graph on step 3, this issue also happens.\n--- Details\nProbably this is a bug on Unity side. ClickSelector on the node seems not to be called.\nIf you select Copy operation on step 3, then this issue doesn't happen. So, system implementation of cancelling context menu have a problem, I guess.",
